# Login refusal with a reason (server/README.md "Character Bazaar"). Live test 2026-10-14: logging in with a character
# listed on the Character Bazaar only showed "connection lost"; the reason was only in the server log. A script that
# refuses a login returns false from onLogin and the engine kicks the player (Player::onPlacedCreature ->
# kickPlayer): everything sent so far, the login packets and any text message, sat in the protocol's output buffer,
# which is dropped when the connection closes. New Lua method player:refuseLogin(message): the login error packet
# (0x14, what the engine's own refusals send through ProtocolGame::disconnectClient) goes out at once with
# Protocol::send, like the client guard's refusal (patch 0021); the caller then returns false from onLogin as before.
# The client shows "Login Error" with the text and goes back to the login screen. Used by
# data/scripts/chaos/bazaar.lua (in the player's language, Chaos.t). Built against the chain 0001-0038.
# Applies after 0001-0038.
diff --git a/src/luascript.cpp b/src/luascript.cpp
--- a/src/luascript.cpp
+++ b/src/luascript.cpp
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include "chat.h"
 #include "player.h"
 #include "clientguard.h"
